        "comments": "The assembly dcRumObtu1.hap1.1 is based on 88x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Two different HiC patterns could be observed on the HiC map during curation, suggesting the species could be an allotetraploid, but works as a functional diploid. The HAP1 file contains one copy of each subgenome. The order and orientation of the scaffolds on Chromosome 16 8.32 Mbp - 11.80 Mbp are uncertain.",
